  "reference_notes": "Chosen Great wood-rush replacement for the explicitly temperate-listed generic woodland groundcover; legacy ID retained, not a claim that the old jungle placeholder already depicted Luzula. Compared KPU basal tuft photograph and RHS flower-panicle photograph with revised current seeds 1, 4 and 7 and all 36 variants. Replaced upright strap rays with 16-22 basal blades arching back toward the forest floor. Spring vegetative tufts are 0.20-0.38 m tall; mature flowering stems are deliberately absent. Compact and spreading crowns retain individual descending blades. At 25 mm, true 10-20 mm blade widths and marginal hairs are unresolved, especially in small tufts. Accepted as stylized spring foliage architecture, not botanical microdetail.",
